WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:06.102
MAID deaths: seventy-six thousand seven hundred and seven between 2016 and 2024.

00:00:06.102 --> 00:00:12.250
Opioid deaths: fifty-three thousand three hundred and eight between 2016 and 2025.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:23.852
Combined: one hundred and twenty-nine thousand seven hundred and eighty-three deaths — exceeding Canada's combined World War I and World War II casualties of one hundred and eleven thousand four hundred.

00:00:23.852 --> 00:00:30.568
In 2024, MAID accounted for five point one percent of all Canadian deaths — one in every twenty.

00:00:30.568 --> 00:00:37.227
The Parliamentary Budget Officer calculated cost savings of one hundred and forty-nine million dollars per year before expansion.

00:00:37.227 --> 00:00:41.488
The derived cost per life: one thousand nine hundred and sixty dollars.

00:00:41.488 --> 00:00:48.420
Article II of the UN Convention on the Prevention and Punishment of the Crime of Genocide defines five prohibited acts.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:52.999
Article 6 of the Rome Statute defines genocide under international criminal law.

00:00:52.999 --> 00:00:56.648
Both have been mapped to Canadian government actions in this analysis.

00:00:56.648 --> 00:00:58.670
The numbers are not ambiguous.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:00.897
The legal framework is not unclear.

00:01:00.897 --> 00:01:03.318
The question is whether anyone will act.
